$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(3,4-Dimethoxy-phenyl)-ethylamine.[11] Borane in THF (10 mL, 1M sol.,
10 mmol) was added to a solution of 2-(3,4-dimethoxyphenyl)acetonitrile
(12, table 3, entry 9) (895 mg, 5.05 mmol) in dry THF (10 mL) at 23°C.
After stirring the mixture at 55°C for 16 h, the mixture was cooled to
0°C and quenched by careful addition of water (1 mL) followed by addition
of conc. HCl (5 mL). After stirring for 1 h at room temperature, the
mixture was diluted with water (25 mL) and made alkaline by addition of
NaOH (2.5 g). The mixture was then extracted with CH2Cl2 (3-times) and
the organic layers were washed with water and brine, dried (Na2SO4) and
concentrated under reduced pressure to give the amine (911 mg, 99%).
2-(3,4-Dimethoxy-phenyl)-ethylamine. Yellow oil, yield (911 mg, 99%). Rf
= 0.25 (dichloromethane/methanol/conc. NH3 (aq.) = 90:9:1); 1H NMR: δH
(400 MHz, CDCl3) = 1.39 (brs, 2 H), 2.71 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 2 H), 2.96 (t, J
= 6.8 Hz, 2 H), 3.87 (s, 3 H), 3.88 (s, 3 H), 6.71 - 6.78 (m, 2 H), 6.82
(d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1 H); MS (ESI): 363 [2M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
