$DATUM 109-63-7
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of β
acetamido ketones derivatives using microwave: A stirred solution of
aldehyde (10 mmol), nitrile (15 mmol), ketone (10 mmol), and BF3/ Et2O (2
mmol) was irradiated in microwave at 70°C till completion of reaction.
Reaction monitored on TLC (mobile phase-20% Ethyl Acetate in Hexane).
After completion of reaction, product was triturated with 3% aqueous
sodium carbonate solution and resulted reaction mass was stirred for 30
min. Reaction mass filtered on Buchner funnel and washed with water (4V)
for twice and suck dried to get the crude product. The crude products
were recrystallized using suitable solvent like ethanol/isopropanol.
Compound 5g, yield 96%. Melting point (°C): Observed = 150-152; Reference
= 153-154.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, microwave irradiation, alternative preparation shown, no
solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient synthesis of β-acetamido ketones using BF3-Et2O. A fertile
approach toward avoiding usage of acetyl chloride
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Darandale, Sunil N.; Kokare, Nagnnath D.; Sangshetti, Jaiprakash N.;
Shinde, Devanand B.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Green Chemistry Letters and Reviews (2012), 5(4), 643-648

